<section id="pf-scope" class="pf-section pf-reveal">
  <p class="pf-step-tag">Step 1 · Outside view</p>
  <h2><span class="pf-section-number">02</span> Look across places and time</h2>
  <p class="pf-prose">
    The outside view scopes candidate trajectories from precedents abroad, earlier conflicts at home and the positions of Swedish actors. Four
    plausible policy directions were identified.
  </p>
  <div class="pf-table-scroll">
    <table class="pf-directions">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Policy direction</th>
          <th scope="col">Examples</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for dir in pf.policy_directions %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">
              {{ dir.title -}}
              <span class="pf-direction-text">{{ dir.asks }}</span>
            </th>
            <td data-label="Examples">{{ dir.where }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="pf-prose pf-actor-summary">
    Rule-keepers favour incentives and voluntary contracts. Rule-switchers propose generation requirements but disagree over which plants should
    qualify.
  </p>
  <div class="pf-drawers">
    <details class="pf-drawer">
      <summary><strong>Across places</strong><span>Six cases, from Ireland’s requirement to Germany’s postponement</span></summary>
      <div class="pf-outside-part">
        <div class="pf-place-choices" role="group" aria-label="Geographic example" hidden>
          {% for o in pf.outside -%}
            <button type="button" data-pf-place="{{ o.code }}" aria-pressed="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">
              {{ o.country }}
            </button>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="pf-spatial-grid">
          <figure class="pf-place-map" hidden>
            <svg id="pf-place-map" viewBox="0 0 440 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="pf-map-title pf-map-description">
              <title id="pf-map-title">Locations in the policy survey</title><desc id="pf-map-description">Five European examples, with the United States in a separate locator. Choose a country using the buttons to read its example.</desc>
            </svg>
            <figcaption class="pf-caption">Policy examples · <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/">Natural Earth</a></figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="pf-place-readings" aria-live="polite">
            {% for o in pf.outside %}
              <article id="pf-place-{{ o.code }}" class="pf-place-reading">
                <p class="pf-caption">{{ o.country }} · {{ o.status }}</p>
                <h4>{{ o.heading }}</h4>
                <p>{{ o.contribution }}</p>
                <p class="pf-take-forward">{{ o.limit }}</p>
              </article>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pf-drawer">
      <summary><strong>Across time</strong><span>Québec, Danish wind compensation and Bensinupproret</span></summary>
      <div class="pf-outside-part">
        <div class="pf-history-examples">
          {% for h in pf.history %}
            <details class="pf-history-example">
              <summary>
                <strong>{{ h.technology }}</strong><span class="pf-caption">{{ h.period }}</span><span>{{ pf.history_previews[h.id] }}</span>
              </summary>
              <p>{{ h.change }}</p>
              <p>{{ h.response }}</p>
              <p class="pf-take-forward">{{ h.method_question }}</p>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
          <details class="pf-history-example">
            <summary>
              <strong>Bensinupproret · Sweden</strong><span class="pf-caption">2019</span><span>{{ pf.history_previews.bensin }}</span>
            </summary>
            <p>{{ pf.historical_mobilisation.text }}</p>
            <p class="pf-take-forward">{{ pf.historical_mobilisation.method_question }}</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pf-drawer" id="pf-actors">
      <summary><strong>What emerges in Sweden</strong><span>Rule-keepers, rule-switchers and those who decide and enforce</span></summary>
      <div class="pf-outside-part">
        <div class="pf-actor-findings">
          {% for finding in pf.actor_previews %}
            <article>
              <h4>{{ finding.title }}</h4>
              <p>{{ finding.text }}</p>
            </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="pf-actor-groups">
          {% for group in pf.actor_groups %}
            <article>
              <h4>{{ group.title }}</h4>
              <p class="pf-caption">{{ group.note }}</p>
              <ul>
                {% for actor_id in group.actors %}
                  {% assign actor = pf.actors | where: 'id', actor_id | first %}
                  <li>
                    <strong>{{ actor.name }}</strong>{{ actor.policy_question }}
                  </li>
                {% endfor %}
              </ul>
            </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="pf-caption pf-actor-roles-note">
          Rule-keepers defend the current policy, rule-switchers seek to change it, and rule-takers adapt without leading support or opposition. Roles
          can change as costs, interests and alliances develop.
        </p>
        <div class="pf-outside-finding">
          <h4>Follow the conflict forward</h4>
          <p>
            AI investment, industrial decarbonisation and household living costs can pull policy in different directions. Follow how parties rank
            these goals, how public opinion develops and which affected groups organise. The same actors may support different rules at the next
            decision.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
  {% include policy-feasibility/next.liquid href='#pf-trajectories' number='03' title='Define comparable trajectories' %}
</section>
